{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology exhibits severe structural deficiencies for D96A EANCOM INVOIC compliance. It models abstract document structure (Header/Detail/Summary) but completely lacks the concrete EDIFACT segment types (BGM, DTM, NAD, LIN, MOA, etc.) that define invoice semantics. The 'flattening' of all organizations into generic classes without qualifier-based distinctions (NAD+BY vs NAD+SU) violates fundamental EDIFACT principles. Coverage is approximately 15-20% of required D96A elements.",

  "completeness_score": 0.18,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "BGM_BeginningOfMessage",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "D96A INVOIC Mandatory. BGM segment (C002/1001 qualifier '380' for invoice) identifies message type and function. Currently completely absent - no way to distinguish invoice from credit note or other message types."
    },
    ", "owl_reviewed_length": 20154, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 0}

